WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.025
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:08.932
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:15.646
Unit eleven: Essay Introductions. Today you will write an introduction with a hook and a thesis.

4
00:00:15.946 --> 00:00:18.656
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.926
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:24.680
Essay.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:28.240
Essay means a piece of writing on one topic.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.118
Write a short essay.

9
00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:32.951
Your turn. Say: Essay.

10
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.697
Essay.

11
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.590
Introduction.

12
00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:42.198
Introduction means the opening part of an essay.

13
00:00:42.783 --> 00:00:44.377
The introduction is short.

14
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:47.996
Your turn. Say: Introduction.

15
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:51.951
Introduction.

16
00:00:52.717 --> 00:00:53.358
Hook.

17
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:57.116
Hook means a first sentence that catches interest.

18
00:00:57.717 --> 00:00:59.345
Start with a strong hook.

19
00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.999
Your turn. Say: Hook.

20
00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:05.486
Hook.

21
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.181
Background.

22
00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:11.065
Background means basic information about a topic.

23
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:12.953
Give some background.

24
00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.773
Your turn. Say: Background.

25
00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:19.611
Background.

26
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:21.351
Thesis.

27
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.779
Thesis means the main argument of an essay.

28
00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:26.965
State your thesis clearly.

29
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.750
Your turn. Say: Thesis.

30
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.636
Thesis.

31
00:01:34.383 --> 00:01:35.442
Statement.

32
00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.181
Statement means a clear sentence of fact or view.

33
00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:41.493
Write a thesis statement.

34
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:44.724
Your turn. Say: Statement.

35
00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:48.556
Statement.

36
00:01:49.317 --> 00:01:50.097
Topic.

37
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:53.211
Topic means the subject of an essay.

38
00:01:53.817 --> 00:01:55.352
Choose a clear topic.

39
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.417
Your turn. Say: Topic.

40
00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:02.128
Topic.

41
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:03.850
Outline.

42
00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:07.465
Outline means to give the main points briefly.

43
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:09.759
Outline your main ideas.

44
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.712
Your turn. Say: Outline.

45
00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:16.626
Outline.

46
00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:20.701
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.666
Visal, how do I start an essay?

48
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:33.567
Start with a hook to catch interest, like a question or a surprising fact. Then give background and end with a thesis statement.

49
00:02:34.683 --> 00:02:36.404
What is a thesis statement?

50
00:02:37.517 --> 00:02:47.181
It is one sentence that gives your main argument. For example, Cities should plant more trees because they clean the air and cool the streets.

51
00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:49.923
How long is an introduction?

52
00:02:51.017 --> 00:02:57.886
Usually three or four sentences. Do not give all your details. Just outline the main points.

53
00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:00.545
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.383 --> 00:03:03.766
Grammar focus: Thesis statement.

55
00:03:04.066 --> 00:03:05.264
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:10.016
Cities should plant more trees because they clean the air and cool the streets.

57
00:03:10.917 --> 00:03:14.449
Schools should teach writing because it builds thinking and confidence.

58
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.919
A thesis states your main argument in one sentence and often previews your reasons.

59
00:03:20.683 --> 00:03:24.404
Be careful! Don't say: My thesis are that trees help.

60
00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.784
Say: My thesis is that trees help.

61
00:03:29.084 --> 00:03:30.503
Thesis is singular.

62
00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.964
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:36.012
Trees in the City.

64
00:03:36.312 --> 00:03:38.950
Bopha writes an essay about trees in the city.

65
00:03:39.933 --> 00:03:42.931
Her hook asks, Have you ever walked in the shade of a tree?

66
00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:46.258
She adds some background about city heat.

67
00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:50.265
Her thesis says that cities should plant more trees.

68
00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:53.963
She outlines two reasons in the last sentence.

69
00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:58.894
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.645
An essay begins with an blank.

71
00:04:01.945 --> 00:04:05.854
A, ending. B, index. C, introduction.

72
00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.806
The answer is C: introduction.

73
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.984
A hook catches the reader's blank.

74
00:04:15.284 --> 00:04:18.450
A, interest. B, bag. C, phone.

75
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.814
The answer is A: interest.

76
00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.683
A thesis is the main blank.

77
00:04:26.983 --> 00:04:30.172
A, page. B, argument. C, title.

78
00:04:33.733 --> 00:04:36.081
The answer is B: argument.

79
00:04:37.217 --> 00:04:39.042
Background gives basic blank.

80
00:04:39.342 --> 00:04:42.926
A, food. B, music. C, information.

81
00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:48.803
The answer is C: information.

82
00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:51.683
Bopha's topic is blank.

83
00:04:51.983 --> 00:04:55.659
A, trees. B, cars. C, coins.

84
00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.536
The answer is A: trees.

85
00:05:02.733 --> 00:05:05.943
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:06.783 --> 00:05:08.481
How do you write an introduction?

87
00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:18.760
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:28.914
I start with a hook such as a question. Then I give a little background. I finish with a thesis statement that shows my main argument and my reasons.

89
00:05:29.214 --> 00:05:30.784
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:31.683 --> 00:05:35.462
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and thesis statement.

91
00:05:35.762 --> 00:05:41.154
Today's value is eloquence. Choose your words with care, and speak to persuade honestly.

92
00:05:41.454 --> 00:05:44.176
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

93
00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:47.848
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

